    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T03:01:12Z",
    "body": "Independent confirmation from the M5 session (while refreshing #517): this reproduces on plain upstream main 64506ff5 on macOS, without any #416/#417 code. A minimal repro uses `tests/tormach_lathe_support`: `thread_world_with(false, ThreadHand::Right, 25.4/12.0, DEPTH)` gives a TH1 with 12 off-lattice coordinates at 12 TPI. Create TH2 with the same params, and TH2 reads Ok. After `project::save` and `project::load` into a fresh world, TH2 reads Stale (\"operation 'TH1' ahead of it in the program changed\"). The 2.0 mm pitch fixture lands on the lattice on macOS, which is why #516 couldn't reproduce it there. Flank, alternating and constant-area plans are off-lattice on every platform. #516 and #517 now pin `rest::prior_digest` equality across save/load and will go green once this lands.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
